%% state: CURRENT
%% abstraction: runtime-sequence
%% question: How does one posting request become an atomic ledger result or rollback?
%% owner: funds-core maintainers
%% arc42: architecture/arc42/06-runtime-view.md
%% adrs: ADR-0002, ADR-0004, ADR-0006
%% last_verified: 2026-09-01
sequenceDiagram
  participant Caller
  participant Service as PostingService
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  Caller->>Service: typed command + request hash
  Service->>Service: validate request hash
  Service->>DB: begin serializable transaction
  Service->>DB: acquire idempotency lock
  Service->>DB: acquire account locks
  Service->>Service: validate book, period, journal, amounts
  Service->>DB: write immutable journal and postings
  Service->>DB: update projections and balances
  Service->>DB: write outbox intent
  Service->>DB: complete idempotency result
  alt all validation and writes succeed
    Service->>DB: commit
    Service-->>Caller: completed result
  else validation or persistence fails
    Service->>DB: rollback
    Service-->>Caller: failure
  end
